codex-run-8.log:112:   - Problem: `.mlbl` (the "PWR" label) sits immediately left of the meter bar; `#hint` spans full width ending near the same spot. On narrow viewports they collide with no gap — visible in `shots/mobile.png`, `shots/wind-390.png`, `shots/task5-held-390.png` as "...PICK PUSH / NORMAL / KOBEPWR" running together.
codex-run-8.log:153:16. **"KOBE" as a throw-height label is undocumented flavor text.** (`#height-choice` buttons, `index.html:107`) PUSH/NORMAL are self-explanatory; "KOBE" (high lob, named for the fadeaway) requires outside knowledge of the reference to understand it means "high arc." Low priority given the game's playful tone, but a one-word subtitle or distinct icon per button would remove the ambiguity without breaking the joke.
codex-run-8.log:159:19. **Height-choice buttons (PUSH/NORMAL/KOBE) don't indicate whose turn's arc they're setting when height differs per player.** (`M.heights[thrower()]=M.arc` at `index.html:932`) Each player can have an independent default arc, but the UI only shows one active/yellow-highlighted button (the shared `#height-choice` row) with no per-player memory indicator — so switching from Red's turn to Blue's turn, the highlighted button silently represents a different stored value. Minor but worth a glance: confirm `renderHud()` re-syncs the highlighted button to `M.heights[thrower()]` on turn change (it currently keys off `M.arc`, which is shared global state, not the per-player array) — worth double-checking this doesn't desync in 2P.
